dracut-sshd (0.7.1-5~eugenesan~resolute3) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Build the source package as "3.0 (native)" rather than "3.0 (git)".

    The package ships this fork's four modules and upstream's tarball does
    not contain them, so a hand-built orig tarball had to be regenerated
    for every upload. That was the status quo, and the previous attempt at
    fixing it - "3.0 (git)" - replaced the tarball with a git bundle. That
    removes the hand-built tarball but is awkward in the way that matters
    here: the bundle has to sit beside the .dsc for dput to find it, and
    Launchpad then has to consume a bundle rather than a tarball.

    "3.0 (native)" has neither problem. There is no orig component at
    all: dpkg-source puts the whole tree, debian/ included, into a single
    dracut-sshd_<version>.tar.xz next to the .dsc, which is what dput and
    every other Debian upload tool expect. For a package this size that is
    the simpler arrangement and the one worth having.

    debian/gbp.conf goes with the format it was written for: tagging and
    git-buildpackage have no role in a native build.

    NB: dpkg-source prints "native package version may not have a
    revision" on every build, because the version carries the hyphen
    that otherwise separates upstream from revision. It is a warning
    only - the build succeeds and the upload is valid - and recording the
    upstream base and the fork release counters is worth keeping even
    though a native package has no upstream tarball to tell them apart
    from.

  * debian/watch stays deleted, as in the previous version. It tracked
    gsauthof/dracut-sshd's tags, which made sense while the orig tarball
    was upstream's and is actively harmful now: the next automatic bump
    would fetch an upstream tarball with none of the fork's modules and
    produce a build failure.

  * debian/control: Homepage and the previously commented-out
    Vcs-Browser/Vcs-Git now point at this fork rather than upstream, and
    the Vcs fields are enabled so that Launchpad can offer to import from
    git.

  * debian/upstream/metadata: Repository, Repository-Browse and
    Documentation repointed at this fork, Bug-Submit here as well, but
    Bug-Database left on gsauthof/dracut-sshd, since that is still where
    a bug in 46sshd belongs.

 -- Eugene San (eugenesan) <eugenesan@gmail.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:22:05 -0700

dracut-sshd (0.7.1-5~eugenesan~resolute2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * debian/dracut-sshd.dirs: list 30network-manager-wireless. The package
    installs into that module directory exactly as it does for the other
    four, but .dirs had never named it. The module has been absent from
    the file since the initial release, and the rework in 2-1 added
    45netplan to it without adding 30network-manager-wireless, so the
    omission has outlived every restructuring of debian/ since.
    No functional change: dh_install creates the directory when it
    places module-setup.sh, and every directory listed here receives a
    file anyway. This only makes .dirs describe what the package owns.

