dracut-sshd (0.7.1-5~eugenesan~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Move the fork's own content out of debian/ and into the source tree
    proper. debian/ was carrying eight files that are not packaging at
    all - four dracut modules, the telegram-send script, the dracut
    drop-in, the bot token example and the module documentation - and
    the paths actively misled about that: debian/dracut/telegram-send/
    telegram-send.service is a systemd unit, not packaging. Each dracut
    module is now a top-level directory named for the number dracut
    orders it by, next to upstream's 46sshd, which is how upstream
    already models a module and what makes them usable without apt:

      debian/dracut/netplan/                    -> 45netplan/
      debian/dracut/network-manager-wireless/  -> 30network-manager-wireless/
      debian/dracut/telegram-send/              -> 47telegram-send/
      debian/dracut/unlock-root/                -> 82unlock-root/
      debian/bin/telegram-send                  -> 47telegram-send/telegram-send
      debian/config/sshd.conf                   -> example/90-sshd-ubuntu.conf
      debian/config/.telegram_bot               -> example/telegram-send.conf
      debian/readme.dracut-modules.txt          -> readme.dracut-modules.txt

  * 47telegram-send is now self-contained. Its module-setup.sh already
    preferred ${moddir}/telegram-send over the installed copy, but the
    script lived in debian/bin, so the preference could never fire and a
    standalone install had nothing to pick up. It now sits next to the
    units it installs, so copying that one directory in is enough.

  * Two installed files are renamed, which is the user-visible part of
    this change:

      /etc/dracut.conf.d/sshd.conf
        -> /etc/dracut.conf.d/90-sshd-ubuntu.conf
      /usr/share/doc/dracut-sshd/examples/.telegram_bot
        -> /usr/share/doc/dracut-sshd/examples/telegram-send.conf

    The drop-in keeps its contents. The token example is unchanged apart
    from a comment header: it still has to be copied to /root/.telegram_bot
    before update-initramfs, and the module still skips itself silently if
    that file is absent.

 -- Eugene San (eugenesan) <eugenesan@gmail.com>  Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:05:00 -0700

dracut-sshd (0.7.1-4~eugenesan~resolute4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Fix a stale TELEGRAM_MAX_WAIT in the documentation. Both
    debian/dracut/telegram-send/telegram-send.timer and
    debian/readme.dracut-modules.txt still said the service waits
    300s, left over from before the previous version lowered it to
    60s to keep the notification off the boot's critical path. The
    script's own default is genuinely 300s, which is probably why
    this survived; the timer comment now says so explicitly.

